! v0.72.0 test: re-use cached Hessian via %read_hess.
!
! Reads the .hess file written by test_v072_hcn_tsfreq.inp (which
! must have been run first; the test runner script enforces order).
!
! Same input geometry, same method/basis/spin -- the reader's
! consistency check should accept the file and the optimizer should
! converge to the same TS in the same number of steps as the
! corresponding "auto-Hessian" path.
!
! This exercises Path A of the JOB_OPT_TS dispatcher: load cached
! Cartesian Hessian, skip the upfront freq computation entirely,
! jump straight into P-RFO.  Practical use case: user runs %job
! freq once to inspect modes in Molden, picks the right %ts_mode
! index, then runs %job ts %read_hess <file>.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     ts
%charge  0
%mult    1
%hess_method  analytical
%ts_mode 1
%read_hess test_v072_hcn_tsfreq.hess
%geom_maxiter 80
%geom angstrom
C   -0.55  -0.20   0.00
N    0.55  -0.20   0.00
H    0.00   0.95   0.00
*end
